      },
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# 🌍 Plate Tectonics\n\n### The Engine That Reshapes Earth\n\nThe Earth's **lithosphere** is broken into massive tectonic plates that slowly drift across the planet. Their movement creates **mountains**, **volcanoes**, **earthquakes**, and **ocean basins**, continuously recycling and reshaping the surface over millions of years.\n\n> *A planet that appears solid is, in reality, always in motion.*",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1784948047972,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
